Based on the provided content, it seems that the malicious software in question is not a package from a package manager, but rather a flaw in the LiteSpeed Cache plugin for WordPress. Here is the extracted information:

[
    {
        "Package Name": "LiteSpeed Cache Plugin",
        "Package Version": "5.7",
        "Date of Discovery": "October 2023",
        "Method of Attack": "Unauthorized site-wide stored cross-site scripting (XSS) problem due to lack of input sanitization by users and escaping output",
        "Discoverer": "Patchstack",
        "Impacted Systems": ["WordPress"],
        "Attack Vector": "Privilege escalation on a WordPress site and steal any information by sending a single HTTP request",
        "Indicators of Compromise": {
            "CVE ID": ["CVE 2023-40000", "CVE-2023-4372"],
            "Flaw": ["Lack of input sanitization", "escaping output"],
            "Fix Version": "5.7.0.1"
        }
    }
]